Topic 12 – Constructors
Objective: Object initialization, constructor types, constructor overloading and constructor chaining.
No.	Program	Requirement
01	Default Constructor	Create a class with an explicitly declared default constructor and initialize default values.
02	Compiler-Provided Default	Create a class without any constructor and instantiate it. Observe the default initialization.
03	Parameterized Constructor	Create an Employee class with a parameterized constructor that initializes ID, name and salary.
04	Multiple Objects	Create multiple objects using the same parameterized constructor with different values.
05	Constructor Overloading	Create constructors with different parameter lists in the same class.
06	Two Parameter Constructors	Create a Student class with constructors accepting name only and name plus marks.
07	this Keyword	Use this to differentiate instance variables from constructor parameters.
08	Constructor Chaining Using this()	Invoke one constructor from another constructor in the same class.
09	Constructor Chaining Using super()	Create parent and child classes and invoke the parent constructor from the child constructor.
10	Constructor-Based Object Initialization	Create a TestConfiguration class that initializes browser name, URL and timeout through constructors.